.TH DANBYEQNALL 1
.SH NAME
danbyeqnall \- redo every Danby example surveyed so far as eqn(7), not just one per family
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danbyeqnall
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Danbyeqnall
extends
.IR danbyeqntest (1)
(one representative formula per Danby family) to every model actually
named and surveyed across the whole
.I "danby-tks-plan"
design thread: all 17
.B Trajectory
plugins, both
.B Populationmodel
examples, and both
.B Twospecies
examples.
.PP
Every
.B Trajectory
check compares the eqn-translated formula against the real plugin's own
oracle function
.RB ( ballistics->acceleration
or
.BR atmosphere->drag2 ),
called directly with that plugin's own real
.B parameter()
values \(em not a hand-computed expected number, which would only prove
arithmetic, not that this
.I is
the plugin's own physics.
.TP
.B "11 plugins, one shared call form"
.RB ( ballistics ", " basketball ", " badminton ", " baseballpitch ", "
.BR discus ", " flyball ", " golfdrive ", " javelin ", "
.BR softballpitch ", " spinningball ")"
all call
.B ballistics->acceleration()
with the same argument shape, different real constants only.
.B Spinningball
doesn't even load the
.B Ballistics
module \(em the same formula is written out inline in its own
.BR rhs() ,
checked against the same oracle since the two compute identically.
.TP
.B "tabletennis, knuckleball, skijump"
Real per-plugin variations on the same formula, not just different
constants:
.B tabletennis
negates lift (a topspin convention);
.B knuckleball
computes a time-dependent flutter force
.RI ( "amplitude sin( omega t )" )
as its own small eqn expression first, then feeds the result into the
same
.I ay
formula as an ordinary bound value;
.B skijump
wind-shifts
.I vx
.RI ( "relativevx = vx + wind" )
before the same acceleration call. Each is checked exactly as its own
real plugin computes it, chaining compiled eqn expressions the way
.IR doc/danby-tks-plan.md 's
own hoc-adapter design calls for.
.TP
.B "icbmrange, skylab"
The
.B atmosphere->drag2
formula (density, then a shared drag factor, then two components),
each step its own eqn expression, checked against the real function.
Assumes altitude
.RI \(>= 0
(density()'s own one piecewise clamp \(em out of scope, same reasoning
as
.IR danbyeqntest (1)'s
pendulum friction term).
.B Reentry
and
.B rocket2d
also use
.B atmosphere->drag2 ,
but add their own piecewise terms (a speed>0 lift correction; a
burn-time cutoff in
.BR propulsion->thrustacceleration )
\(em named here, not silently skipped, but not checked.
.PP
.B Populationmodel
and
.B Twospecies
have no separate oracle module (their rhs is inline in the plugin
itself), so those checks use hand-computed values, same as
.IR danbyeqntest (1):
.B vaccination
(identical SIR dynamics to
.B epidemic ,
plus a real, unomitted
.RI "d(vaccinated)=0"
line) and
.B competition
(a genuinely different Lotka-Volterra variant \(em real competition,
not predator-prey \(em at its own real default parameters).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/danbyeqnall.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danbyeqntest (1),
.IR eqn2hoc (2),
.IR hoc (2)
.SH BUGS
Covers every model named across the design thread except Mechanism's
.B simplependulum
(already in
.IR danbyeqntest (1),
not repeated) and the Flight3d family
.RB ( soccerkick ", " cricketbowl ", " cricketswing ", " badfootball ,
all using
.BR ballistics->acceleration3 ,
3-D drag+Magnus) \(em out of scope here since Flight3d was never named
in the design thread this redo follows.
.PP
Each Trajectory state is a single representative
.RI ( vx , vy ,
altitude) point, not a trajectory integrated over time \(em this
checks that the per-step acceleration formula is right, not that a
full simulation run matches.
